{"id": "EUVD-2026-93110", "enisaUuid": "8493e10a-1a67-337e-bbdd-b2e6458671b6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: refuse to make a monitor active when it has no queue\n\nA monitor interface only gets a TXQ if it's created active, and one can't\nbe added later. Setting the flag on a down interface is still allowed, so\nthe driver is handed a monitor with no queue. ath9k dereferences it:\n\n  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000066\n  RIP: 0010:ath_tx_node_init+0x49/0x170 [ath9k]\n   ath9k_add_interface+0x10c/0x140 [ath9k]\n   drv_add_interface+0x54/0x250 [mac80211]\n   ieee80211_do_open+0x32f/0x800 [mac80211]\n\nReached with CAP_NET_ADMIN by \"iw dev X set monitor active\" followed by\n\"ip link set X up\". RTNL is held, so netlink operations block behind it.\n\nRefuse the flag when there is no queue to give.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7b7d46ec4fa127767931938b282c361c0519af6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abe15e643e576459469867758ae9c586a7bab95d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46c223468537a05a404699771cd3e68532dab5e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b04d6556964ae9f89819b86a0a7801e39c3aae5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-29gw-9f65-5xh9", "CVE-2026-98182"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f512104-80bc-30db-8dc6-46e6d0ede6a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "19683342-4eeb-3b22-9b67-a5826d83a61c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "443d1bd9-7796-3f9d-bb69-31c6952ac18b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79af1f866193de29e65a4dba7d0dab14b0c0ff93 <b7b7d46ec4fa127767931938b282c361c0519af6"}, {"id": "7384cbe7-6a90-32e5-96c5-83ddebfd2777", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "73c018b8-c722-3a03-aa2f-74d70c393e13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79af1f866193de29e65a4dba7d0dab14b0c0ff93 <abe15e643e576459469867758ae9c586a7bab95d"}, {"id": "959e4088-230e-3b2a-aba1-c0344fcf0310", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79af1f866193de29e65a4dba7d0dab14b0c0ff93 <2b04d6556964ae9f89819b86a0a7801e39c3aae5"}, {"id": "9ef08a6f-525f-3f03-84e9-efdd90c30f74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "aa940051-2c45-3764-95d7-9a31de640e77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.15"}, {"id": "bd61e9cb-35d4-30c2-ac69-3cd23093e6f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "79af1f866193de29e65a4dba7d0dab14b0c0ff93 <46c223468537a05a404699771cd3e68532dab5e6"}, {"id": "e89d924a-7835-37af-98fe-09125887299f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0dd7e9d1-99c0-3f99-ad59-ff986bb72800", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}